  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BEL: Social care and dementia support to Jewish communities in Belarus</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Jewish Relief has been working in Belarus since the 1990s in partnership with the local Belarusian organisation Hesed Rakhamim which supports over 2,000 older Jewish people in Minsk who require medical and social support.
The aim of this project is to improve the quality of life of older people living with dementia who are isolated from community life and lack specialist services. The project will also build support networks for those caring for a relative with dementia, increase awareness about dementia to build a more tolerant, dementia-friendly community. Lastly it aims to increase social contact for isolated people living alone by providing befriending services.</narrative>
  </description>
